\f0\b0\fs32 \cf0 Activism, politics, feminism, vindication and a lot of music. 
\f2\b Roc\'edo Saiz 
\f0\b0 is a solo singer as well as part of the groups 
\f2\b Monterrosa and Las Chillers,
\f0\b0  she is also a DJ and communicator. Her speech in favor of diversity and her criticism of heteropatriarchy have made her one of the LGTBIQ+ referents with more character and strength in Spain.
\f3\fs24 \

\f0\fs32 Now she embarks on this new adventure. The dance floor is political, fun is never as innocent as it is painted, and love dramas are rarely a non-transferable experience. Roc\'edo talks about everything that happens before, during and after the dance: disappointments, sex with and without love, toxic relationships, the fullness of being master of your destiny for as many hours as possible, but also the insomnia derived from work stress and lack of money and the need for a certain hedonism to forget everything from time to time.
\f3\fs24 \

\f0\fs32 He has done it with Monterrosa with Eurovision hits and out-of-time ballads, as if we could put together
\f2\b  Tino Casal, La Oreja de Van Gogh, Abba, Astrud, Cecilia and Vengaboys
\f0\b0  to make generational anthems that explain how we feel in 2020, and now he sets out on his own to unite worlds between Monterrosa\'92s sophistication and his living force with Las Chillers. In the summer of 2022 she was the presenter of the fashion show \'91Out of the closet\'92 for the 
\f2\b Hotel W Ibiza 
\f0\b0 and the presenter of the new 
\f2\b Movistar 
\f0\b0 + space \'91La Nevera de Inverfest\'92.
\f3\fs24 \

\f0\fs32 He has participated in numerous festivals such as 
\f2\b Atlantic Fest, Cala Mijas or Culture Business Pride in Tenerife
\f0\b0 with Village People.
\f3\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

