\fs48 \cf0 \cb2 Fashion designer\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb2 Pablo Erroz is one of Spain\'92s most promising fashion designers. Born in Palma de Mallorca and trained in Barcelona, he launched his own label in 2010 after gaining experience in outerwear and leather with Inditex. Erroz\'92s work is characterized by the creation of unisex and timeless pieces aimed at individuals with personality who value ethical fashion and are willing to invest in garments that endure over time. His collections interpret a fusion of street style with easy, sophisticated luxury, adapting to contemporary trends.\cb1 \
\
\cb2 His designs encompass clothing and leather goods with bold, sporty silhouettes, reflecting a craftsmanship approach that harmonizes the past and future. This annual proposal, which merges summer and winter, seeks to eliminate traditional seasons and promote a more mindful and environmentally respectful consumption.\cb1 \
\
\cb2 At just 34 years old, Pablo Erroz has emerged as one of the most influential voices in Spanish fashion, championing the idea that fashion is a communication tool capable of transforming society. His collaboration with Xiaomi seamlessly merges fashion and technology, showcasing products like the Smart Band 8 Pro. Erroz views technology as key to his work, enhancing connectivity and efficiency. For him, fashion is a bridge that connects people and businesses, addressing themes of sustainability and responsible tech usage.\cb1 \
\
\cb2 Notably, Pablo Erroz has designed and supervised the customization of Air Europa\'92s float for the Madrid LGTBIQ+ Pride Parade in 2024. This collaboration reflects the multidisciplinary and collaborative ethos of his fashion house, which has also expanded through partnerships with sectors such as technology and aviation. The float design fuses the identity of Air Europa and Erroz\'92s brand, highlighting elements such as the blue and white of the sky, freedom, and references to iconic cities. This collaboration reinforces the strategic alliances between both entities, allowing them to continue exploring new horizons.\cb1 \
\
\cb2 Surprises at Mercedes-Benz Fashion Week Madrid 2025 with a collection inspired by the vibrant energy of urban hotels. Seasonless, it embraces versatility and a unisex approach, reaffirming its commitment to sustainability by minimizing environmental impact and prioritizing durability and timelessness in every piece.\cb1 \
\
\cb2 Additionally, Erroz has collaborated with prominent brands like Xiaomi and Montblanc, and has been featured in interviews with RTVE and La Raz\'f3n Espa\'f1a, further solidifying his reputation in the fashion industry.\cb1 \
}